# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# `node_modules` first and by a wide margin: copying a host's tree in would defeat the layer that
# resolves the lockfile, and on a machine that ran `pnpm install` with the temporary overrides the
# Phase 18 report describes it would copy in symlinks pointing outside the container entirely.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. The image builds its own; a stale `dist` copied in is the classic "I fixed that"
# deployment.
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
.turbo
**/.turbo

# Secrets and local state. `.env.example` is deliberately not excluded — it is documentation.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.storage
dump.rdb

# History and tooling, which change on every commit and would invalidate every cached layer.
.git
.github
.vscode

# Documentation and specifications. They are the reason this repository is legible and they are not
# part of any image; excluding them keeps a rebuild from re-running on a typo in a report.
docs
prompts
*.md
!README.md
